#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION.rst:2
msgid "CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/include/ENV_VAR.rst:1
msgid ""
"This is a CMake :ref:`Environment Variable <CMake Language Environment "
"Variables>`. Its initial value is taken from the calling process environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION.rst:8
msgid ""
"Environment variable that controls how :manual:`ctest <ctest(1)>` handles "
"cases when there are no tests to run. Possible values are: ``error``, "
"``ignore``, empty or unset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION.rst:12
msgid ""
"The :option:`--no-tests=\\<action\\> <ctest --no-tests>` option to :manual:"
"`ctest <ctest(1)>` overrides this environment variable if both are given."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION.rst:16
msgid ""
"When :option:`ctest --preset` is used, this environment variable, if set, "
"takes precedence over the :preset:`testPresets.execution.noTestsAction` "
"field of the selected test preset. This includes the case where the variable "
"is instead set via the preset's own :preset:`testPresets.environment` field, "
"which is equivalent to setting it in the calling process's environment. An "
"explicit :option:`--no-tests=\\<action\\> <ctest --no-tests>` on the command "
"line takes precedence over all of the above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../envvar/CTEST_NO_TESTS_ACTION.rst:25
msgid ""
"This environment variable, including when set via a test preset's "
"``environment`` field, is also respected when that same preset is used by a :"
"command:`ctest_test` command in a :ref:`CTest Script`. However, in that "
"case, the preset's ``noTestsAction`` field itself has no effect, because :"
"command:`ctest_test` has no equivalent argument to apply it through."
msgstr ""
